# The two pages from the address bar (cavekit-site-data.md R4, T-664): on a web page, the address typed on the system
# keyboard (its ':' from the symbols layer) and Enter: about:logins opens, then about:data, each kept as a picture of
# the shell's look. The other scripts open them through the inject channel, which is not the address bar. The second
# address is typed once the keyboard of the first has gone: until then the field keeps its focus (its clear button
# shows), and a tap on a focused field places the caret instead of selecting the address (Enyo, round
# finger-2026-11-17: "about:loginsabout:data").
id: site-data-address
section: Privacy and site data
item: about:logins and about:data typed into the address bar on the system keyboard open the two pages
shells: enyo mochi mojo
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-card-events.html
kit: cavekit-site-data.md R4
calibrate bar
chrome address
expect keyboard up 8
type-keys about:logins
chrome kb-enter
wait url about:logins 15
wait text page-title "Saved logins" 10
expect keyboard down 8
shoot logins
chrome address
expect keyboard up 8
type-keys about:data
chrome kb-enter
wait url about:data 15
wait text page-title "Site data" 10
shoot data
